<DocsLayout title={title}>
<h1>Function Calling</h1>
<p>Define custom functions that the model can invoke. The model returns a tool call with arguments; your application executes the function and returns the result. Chat Completions nests the definition under <code>function</code>; Responses uses its own flat tool shape.</p>
<pre><code>{`curl -X POST http://localhost:18645/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "grok-4.6",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What is the weather in Seoul?"}],
    "tools": [{
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "get_weather",
        "description": "Get current weather for a location",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "location": {"type": "string", "description": "City name"}
          },
          "required": ["location"]
        }
      }
    }]
  }'`}</code></pre>
<p>For Responses, send a tool such as <code>{`{"type":"function","name":"get_weather","parameters":{...}}`}</code> and return a <code>function_call_output</code> item using the emitted <code>call_id</code>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
